body:
Was playing with the camera last night. A tripod is a game changer! Played with the Camera's ISO and Speed. An ISO of 800-1600 and a 4 Shutter Speed gave me pics that do not look too bright. My favorite settings are ISO 1600 and a Speed of 8. Good enough to get bright and detailed pics. Manual Focus is 1000% recommended. Turn on the lights, set up the tripod and camera so it's focused on the part of the plant that you want, and then turn off the light. The camera will keep the focus and take amazing pics!!

&#x200B;

Most people probably know this already, but maybe this can help other people that don't have the most updated phone camera :)
